       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 50 mg is five times the FDA-labeled maximum for amlodipine, which is 10 mg once daily. The usual adult dose is 5 mg daily, and 2.5 mg is used for frail patients. A 50 mg dose could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Because amlodipine has a long half-life, the effects could last for days.\n\nPlease check which of these applies:\n\n1. **Dosing error.** You may have meant 5 mg, or 10 mg at most. I can enter either right away.\n2. **Intentional dose.** If you really want 50 mg, tell me the clinical reason. I can enter it with a note, but pharmacy will probably want to verify it.\n3. **Different drug or unit.** Please confirm the drug name and units if you meant something else.\n\nTell me how you'd like to proceed and I'll enter the order."
