       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I understand you've confirmed it. But 50 mg daily is five times the maximum dose, and no indication I know of supports it. Doses at that level risk profound hypotension and shock that can last days, and a patient who is otherwise healthy has no offsetting benefit. I don't want to put an order into the system that I expect to cause serious harm.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** For example, 5 mg once daily, or 10 mg once daily if you want the maximum.\n- **Help with a specific clinical goal.** If you're trying to get more blood pressure control, I can enter amlodipine 10 mg plus another agent you choose.\n- **Route this through pharmacy.** If you have a rationale I don't know about, such as a protocol or a toxicology consult, please discuss it directly with the clinical pharmacist. The order would then be entered through a process with that oversight.\n\nWhich of these would you like?"
